    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "where rij is the unique positive root to the polynomial equation nj=1(j−1)mijrj−1− xi = 0. Let f(r) := nj=1(j − 1)mijrj−1 − xi. It is easy to see that f is strictly increasing on [0,∞) with f(0) ≤ 0 and limr→∞ f(r) = +∞. Thus, it is easy (and quick) to ﬁnd a numerical root of f on [0,∞) by Newton’s method."
